{"tool_name":"pasta","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"pasta","identifiers":["biotools:pasta","doi:10.1093/nar/gku399"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"An implementation of the Practical Alignment using Sate and TrAnsitivity) algorithm","home_url":"https://github.com/smirarab/pasta","keywords":["Amyloid","Internet","Intrinsically Disordered Proteins","Peptides","Point Mutation","Protein Structure, Secondary","Sequence Analysis, Protein","Sequence analysis","Protein interactions","Clustering","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":6},"biotools":{"id":"pasta","home":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/pasta2/index.html","summary":"A web server predictor for amyloid aggregation propensity from protein sequences.","addition_date":"2015-11-05T16:59:49Z","last_update_date":"2022-02-10T14:29:09.893185Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"version":["2.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pasta","credit":[{"email":"silvio.tosatto@unipd.it","name":"Silvio Tosatto","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4525-7793","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it"},{"name":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"University of Padua, Department of Biomedical Sciences, BioComputing UP lab","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/pasta2/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein interaction prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2492"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1255"},"format":[{"term":"MHTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3556"}]}]}],"name":"PASTA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gku399","metadata":{"abstract":"The formation of amyloid aggregates upon protein misfolding is related to several devastating degenerative diseases. The propensities of different protein sequences to aggregate into amyloids, how they are enhanced by pathogenic mutations, the presence of aggregation hot spots stabilizing pathological interactions, the establishing of cross-amyloid interactions between co-aggregating proteins, all rely at the molecular level on the stability of the amyloid cross-beta structure. Our redesigned server, PASTA 2.0, provides a versatile platform where all of these different features can be easily predicted on a genomic scale given input sequences. The server provides other pieces of information, such as intrinsic disorder and secondary structure predictions, that complement the aggregation data. The PASTA 2.0 energy function evaluates the stability of putative cross-beta pairings between different sequence stretches. It was re-derived on a larger dataset of globular protein domains. The resulting algorithm was benchmarked on comprehensive peptide and protein test sets, leading to improved, state-of-the-art results with more amyloid forming regions correctly detected at high specificity. The PASTA 2.0 server can be accessed at http://protein.bio.unipd.it/pasta2/. \u00a9 2014 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Seno F."},{"name":"Tosatto S.C.E."},{"name":"Trovato A."},{"name":"Walsh I."}],"citationCount":203,"date":"2014-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"PASTA 2.0: An improved server for protein aggregation prediction"},"pmcid":"PMC4086119","pmid":"24848016","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"PASTA","home":"https://bio.tools/pasta